  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 clearly outperforms scgpt in singleprofile multimodal settings (~0.53 vs ~0.43 accuracy), and multiprofile + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion is the strongest configuration (config_042: 0.725 acc). However, all multiprofile experiments so far use scvi_n200; we have zero data on how scgpt performs in the multiprofile regime. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the aggregation step (transformer over multiple profiles) compensates for a weaker per-profile RNA representation, potentially narrowing or eliminating the scvi_n200 advantage. This experiment (config_001: scgpt, multiprofile, transformer, weighted) changes only the RNA encoder relative to config_042, cleanly isolating the RNA encoder effect in the multiprofile regime. If scgpt is close to scvi_n200 here, it reveals that profile-level aggregation mitigates representation quality and opens a cheaper design space; if it is substantially worse, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and we can focus remaining budget on image encoder and fusion refinements. This single-variable comparison is the highest-information experiment available under the limited budget."
}

